            <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">What it is</h2>
              <p>Search Engine Optimization is the practice of making a website earn higher placement in organic (unpaid) search results. Unlike paid ads, SEO traffic doesn't cost per click — once you rank, every visitor is essentially free.</p>
              <p><strong>SEO has 3 main pillars:</strong> (1) <strong>Technical SEO</strong> — site speed, crawlability, schema markup, mobile experience; (2) <strong>On-page SEO</strong> — headlines, content quality, internal linking, keyword targeting; (3) <strong>Off-page SEO</strong> — backlinks, brand mentions, trust signals.</p>
              <p>Modern SEO in 2026 is increasingly about being a real authority on a topic — Google's algorithms reward genuine expertise (E-E-A-T: Experience, Expertise, Authoritativeness, Trust). Tricks and shortcuts that worked in 2015 actively hurt today.</p>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">Real example</h2>
              <p>An e-commerce store that ranks #1 for 'organic cotton baby clothes' gets 2,000 visits/month from Google with zero ad spend. The same brand bidding on that keyword in Google Ads might pay USD 3/click × 2,000 visits = USD 6,000/month for the same traffic.</p>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">How Apex Marketings uses this</h2>
